source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Measure how well mxr sorts mail: today's classifier against labelled scenarios

Usage: mxr classify [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  report  Count stored fallback decisions, grouped by home, sender kind and rule
  eval    Grade the mail already in this mailbox against labelled scenarios: how often today's rules agree on who sent it, which mode it goes to and whether it makes a record; for what an email asks of you, precision and recall per kind of ask and how often the amount, due date and counterparty are exactly right; and every email they get wrong. Read-only and local. Run `mxr demo` first to get mail with labels
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT>  Limit to one account; the default covers every account
      --format <FORMAT>    [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help               Print help
